{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Between the evenings, a pesach to HaShem.</b> Meaning: the portion pertaining to HaShem from the paschal sacrifice — which is the giving of the blood and the burning of fats — shall be between the evenings; but the portion pertaining to Israel — which is the eating of the flesh — shall be on the night of the fifteenth, with unleavened bread and bitter herbs. Further, it intends in saying <b>a pesach to HaShem</b>, that the Egyptian pesach — which is the first pesach — they performed out of love for the benefactor and the efficacious agent: the benefactor, concerning whom they of blessed memory said (Exodus Rabbah 19) that Moses' pesach was fragranced with the breezes of Garden of Eden — and see what I explained in parashat Bo (Exodus 12:43) — and the efficacious agent that caused the Destroyer to pass over their houses. But here it says that the pesach of all generations they shall perform in the name of HaShem, even though it contains neither of those two things."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:24.120667606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}